internal/readline is a vendored fork of ergochat/readline v0.1.3
(https://github.com/ergochat/readline), itself a fork of chzyer/readline. It is
distributed under the MIT License in the adjacent LICENSE file
(Copyright (c) 2015 Chzyer).

Strument's changes to the vendored copy:

  * Non-destructive, single-write redraw (runebuf.go). Each refresh overwrites
    the prompt and buffer cells in place and only then clears the remainder
    with \e[K / \e[J, instead of clearing before repainting — so the prompt no
    longer flickers on slow or remote terminals. The technique is adapted from
    bestline by Justine Tunney (https://github.com/jart/bestline), a descendant
    of antirez's linenoise. No bestline code is copied; only its redraw
    algorithm is reused. bestline is distributed under the 2-clause BSD License:

        Copyright (c) 2018-2021 Justine Tunney <jtunney@gmail.com>
        Copyright (c) 2010-2016 Salvatore Sanfilippo <antirez@gmail.com>
        Copyright (c) 2010-2013 Pieter Noordhuis <pcnoordhuis@gmail.com>

        Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
        modification, are permitted provided that redistributions retain the
        above copyright notice, this list of conditions, and the following
        disclaimer. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
        KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.

  * Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right move by word (terminal.go), matching Alt+arrow and
    aider's prompt_toolkit bindings.

  * The input-history file is created 0600 rather than upstream's 0666
    (history.go), matching ~/.bash_history. It is set in both places that open
    it: the rewrite path writes a temp file and renames over the original, which
    replaces the inode, so a mode set once on the file would not survive.
